# Marketing website — mission & positioning

**Scope:** Main marketing site only (`frontend/` excluding `frontend/src/sales-portal/**`). Do not change Sales Portal product copy or flows unless explicitly asked.

**Full brief:** `frontend/docs/marketing-website-brief.md`

## What Shyara Marketing is (now)

We **only build websites** for local and small businesses. We are not a general digital marketing agency. Removed from public positioning: social media management, ads campaign management, app development, offers/pricing pages, and plan cards.

## Mission (lead every story)

**Turn India digital** — help everyday businesses get online so new customers can find them, trust them, and walk in.

Frame copy around: people search online before they visit; a professional website builds trust; being invisible on Google and in AI answers (ChatGPT, Gemini) means losing customers to competitors who show up.

## Who we serve

B2C and local businesses, including: restaurants, clinics & healthcare, gyms, coaching classes, automobile garages, car/bike washes, and similar “find us → visit us” businesses.

## What clients actually care about (sell outcomes, not gimmicks)

Lead with real business value:

- **Found online** — Google search visibility, local SEO, maps presence
- **SEO** — rank for what their customers search
- **AEO / GEO** — answer-engine & generative-engine optimization so AI assistants can recommend them by name when asked
- **Trust** — credible site, clear info (hours, location, services, contact)
- **More customers** — inquiries, calls, WhatsApp, footfall

Avoid vague agency fluff (“growth hacking”, “360° solutions”) unless tied to a concrete outcome.

## Voice & UX

- Mission-driven, clear, confident — not price-led or discount-led
- Less text, more proof: samples, outcomes, before/after search visibility where possible
- Primary CTA: start a conversation (WhatsApp) about getting their business online
- No public ₹ pricing or “offers” on the marketing site

## Ripples on every marketing change

When editing routes, nav, footer, SEO, or structured data:

- Remove or redirect dead service URLs (SMM, ads, apps, offers)
- Update `AppRoutes.tsx`, `Header.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`, `prerender.mjs`, and `StructuredData.tsx` together
- Keep website samples/portfolio as proof of vertical fit (restaurant, clinic, gym, etc.)
- Service detail pages should reflect **website development + discoverability** only

## Design direction (overhaul)

Highly animated, color-rich, immersive — see prior overhaul plan — but **content must always serve the mission above**, not generic “creative agency” tropes.
